# An `as name` binding a branch arm never reads is refused in the FRONT END, at the
# arm (2026-09-16). Until then Zig refused the emitted switch capture ("unused
# capture") and the source map returned it as a Zebra error with a line and NO column
# -- the one diagnostic `diag-columns` could not see, because it was not ours.
# `on Shape.circle` without `as` is the fix; a guarded arm is exempt (the guard reads
# the binding), and `as _` says "don't care" explicitly.
#
#   branch_unused_binding_test.zbr:N:C: error: unused binding 'r' in this arm: use it, or write the arm without `as r`
union Shape
    circle: int
    square: int

def main()
    var s = Shape.circle(3)
    branch s
        on Shape.circle as r
            print("circle")
        on Shape.square as q
            print(q)
